:: Entrance {"position":"25,125","size":"100,100"}
You stand at the bottom of a ladder into a dark cellar.

The air smells stale and dusty, as if it hasn't been moved in years.

<!-- Hotspot pattern: the hook is rerun after every use, so it always reflects current world state. -->\
|doorspot>[(if: $door_locked is true)[There is a (link-repeat: "door")[(replace: ?doorresult)[($useOn: "the iron lock", (dm: "rusty-key", "use-key-door"), "The door is locked and requires a key.")(rerun: ?doorspot)]] with a small, iron lock.]\
(else:)[There is an unlocked [[door->Storeroom]].]]
|doorresult>[]
(if: $wine_door_bolted)[A heavy door on the far wall is bolted from the other side.]\
(else:)[A [[heavy door->Wine Cellar]] on the far wall stands unbolted.]
(if: ($has: "heartstone"))[[[Escape->Escape]] with the Heartstone!]


:: use-key-door [use] {"position":"25,250","size":"100,100"}
($move: "rusty-key", "gone")(set: $door_locked to false)\
You unlock the door with the Rusty Key.


:: Storeroom {"position":"150,125","size":"100,100"}
You stand in a musky Storeroom. The walls are lined with casks and barrels filled with long-forgotten wine.

(if: $where's hammer is "Storeroom")[There is a hammer resting on the table.]<hammer|
(click-replace: ?hammer)[You take the hammer.\
  <script>pushEvent('Story', 'Hammer', 'Take')</script>\
  ($move: "hammer", "player")\
]

|wallspot>[(if: $wall_intact is true)[Some of the (link-repeat: "bricks")[(replace: ?wallresult)[($useOn: "the loose bricks", (dm: "hammer", "use-hammer-bricks"), "The brick wall sounds hollow, but you cannot budge it with your bare hands.")(rerun: ?wallspot)]] in the wall look loose.]\
(else-if: $collapsing)[Rubble chokes the passage behind the broken wall. The crawlway has collapsed.]\
(else:)[The broken wall reveals a [[dark passage->Crawlway1-dark]].]]
|wallresult>[]

There is a [[door->Entrance]] back to the entrance.


:: use-hammer-bricks [use]
(set: $wall_intact to false)\
*Slam* Bricks fly and crumble under your hammer.


:: Wine Cellar
(set: $thud_lvl to 1)
A long, vaulted wine cellar. Racks of dusty casks line both walls, their labels long since rotted away. In the floor, iron rungs lead down a narrow drain shaft.

Cut into the end of one rack is a ($reveal: "wine-mark", "vintner's mark", ": ''three notches beside a small flame''").

|winespot>[(if: $wine_door_bolted)[A heavy door at the far end is bolted from this side. (link-repeat: "Draw the bolt")[(replace: ?wineresult)[(set: $wine_door_bolted to false)You draw back the stiff iron bolt with a screech.(rerun: ?winespot)]]]\
(else:)[The heavy [[door->Entrance]] at the far end stands unbolted.]]
|wineresult>[]

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

[[Climb down the shaft->Cistern]]


:: Escape [noInvDisplay noInvLink noTick]
<script>pushEvent('Story', 'Finish', 'Escape')</script>\
You climb out into the night air and run swiftly from the rickety house, still swaying in the wind like a dying animal.

You clutch the Heartstone tightly to your chest. You feel its warmth, and try to forget the Dark Cellar you've left behind.

You Win!
